SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"World Bank Deepens Commitment to Building Human Capital and Inclusive Development in the Democratic Republic of Congo","publisher":"World Bank","publication_date":"2022-02-22","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/press-release/2022/02/22/world-bank-deepens-commitment-to-building-human-capital-and-inclusive-development-in-the-democratic-republic-of-congo","claim":"The 2022-2026 Country Partnership Framework supports the DRC government’s strategic priorities, emphasizes human development and stronger basic services, and targets poor, vulnerable, and conflict-affected people through a countrywide social safety net.","locator":"lines 146-155","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official World Bank press release with dated, explicit program language and financing details.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 and explicit 2022-2026 framework","ruler_attribution":"Partial: the document reflects government strategic priorities under Tshisekedi, but implementation is jointly shaped by World Bank financing and technical design.","contrary_evidence":["The same release says poverty is rising and governance is weak, so this is an agenda and financing framework rather than proof of delivery."],"lenses":["8B.1","8B.2","8B.6","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Réunion d'évaluation du programme de développement à la base des 145 territoires présidée ce jour par le chef de l'état.","publisher":"Présidence RDC","publication_date":"2022-09-15","url":"https://www.presidence.cd/actualite-detail/actualite/reunion_devaluation_du_programme_de_developpement_a_la_base_des_145_territoires_presidee_ce_jour_par_le_chef_de_letat","claim":"Tshisekedi chaired an evaluation meeting on the 145-territories development program; officials said the identified projects were ready and the plan would build hospitals, administrative buildings, and other infrastructure across the country.","locator":"lines 71-74","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary presidential page with a dated meeting summary and concrete project description.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022","ruler_attribution":"Direct: the source attributes the meeting to Tshisekedi and reports his oversight of the program, though completion is not shown.","contrary_evidence":["The page says projects were ready and the launch was imminent, which shows preparation more than completed delivery."],"lenses":["8B.1","8B.2","8B.6"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"RDC- Programme de développement de 145 territoires : le gouvernement signe deux protocoles d'accord avec l'IITA","publisher":"Actualite.cd","publication_date":"2022-02-01","url":"https://actualite.cd/index.php/2022/02/01/rdc-programme-de-developpement-de-145-territoires-le-gouvernement-signe-deux-protocoles","claim":"Tshisekedi wanted acceleration of the 145-territories development program, and the government signed two protocols with IITA to support the agricultural transformation component and rapid-start activities.","locator":"lines 90-91","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous local reporting with clear attribution and procedural detail, but not a primary government text.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022","ruler_attribution":"Direct but partial: the report attributes the acceleration push to Tshisekedi, while the concrete implementation work was handled by ministries and IITA.","contrary_evidence":["Signing protocols is a setup step; the article does not itself prove field execution in 2022."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.4","8B.6"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"ANSER lance un nouveau lot d’avis d’appels d’offres relatifs au volet électrification du PDL-145 au profit du Nord-Kivu, Sud-Kivu, Nord-Ubangi et l’espace Grand Kasaï","publisher":"Actualite.cd","publication_date":"2022-09-15","url":"https://actualite.cd/2022/09/15/anser-lance-un-nouveau-lot-davis-dappels-doffres-relatifs-au-volet-electrification-du","claim":"ANSER launched 11 tenders for the PDL-145 rural electrification component, including three hydroelectric plants and eight solar photovoltaic plants in specific territories.","locator":"lines 113-120","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Local reporting with a specific procurement announcement and concrete project list.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022","ruler_attribution":"Direct but partial: the article ties the tenders to the president’s development vision, but execution still depends on procurement and implementation follow-through.","contrary_evidence":["Tenders are not completed projects; the article shows procurement initiation rather than finished electrification."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.4","8B.6"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Compte rendu de la soixante-seizième réunion du Conseil des Ministres","publisher":"Présidence RDC","publication_date":"2022-11-13","url":"https://www.presidence.cd/conseil-de-ministres/compte_rendu_de_la_soixante_seizieme_reunion_du_conseil_des_ministres","claim":"Tshisekedi praised the creation of a National Solidarity and Humanitarian Catastrophe Management Fund, ordered the government to equip it with adequate resources, and pushed a formal monitoring mechanism for the prevention-resilience strategy.","locator":"lines 85-105","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary presidential council minutes with explicit instructions and institutional follow-up steps.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022","ruler_attribution":"Direct: the source records Tshisekedi’s own instructions to the government, though it still shows setup and coordination more than delivered outcomes.","contrary_evidence":["The source is mainly about creating mechanisms and ordering reports; it does not prove the fund had materially improved outcomes by year-end."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.3","8B.5","8B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Compte rendu de la soixante-septième réunion du Conseil des Ministres","publisher":"Présidence RDC","publication_date":"2022-09-02","url":"https://presidence.cd/actualite-detail/actualite/compte_rendu_de_la_soixante_septieme_reunion_du_conseil_des_ministres","claim":"After the swearing-in of 73 magistrates, Tshisekedi stressed serving the nation rather than themselves, reaffirmed judicial independence, and ordered public-finance governance and payroll reforms.","locator":"search snippet lines 72-105","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary presidential communication with a dated, specific institutional directive.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022","ruler_attribution":"Direct: the source quotes Tshisekedi’s instructions and reform emphasis, though downstream implementation is not independently demonstrated here.","contrary_evidence":["This shows directive-setting, not completed implementation or measurable results."],"lenses":["8B.4","8B.5","8B.6","8B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Strengthening the Social Contract: Working towards safer and more inclusive schooling in Democratic Republic of Congo","publisher":"World Bank","publication_date":"2022-06-08","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/opinion/2022/06/08/strengthening-the-social-contract-working-towards-safer-and-more-inclusive-schooling-in-democratic-republic-of-congo","claim":"Free primary education expanded enrollment to 3 million more children; the Allo Ecole grievance hotline became functional nationwide; 20,000 school focal points were appointed and trained; and roughly 60,000 more primary teachers began receiving salaries.","locator":"lines 53-64","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official World Bank article with concrete implementation and output figures tied to a named government program.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 with direct reference to the 2019-2022 rollout","ruler_attribution":"Partial to direct: the article attributes the policy to the DRC government under Tshisekedi-era reforms, but delivery is also heavily World Bank-financed and implemented through sector systems.","contrary_evidence":["The article is a donor-written opinion piece and several gains began before 2022, so it is supportive but not a clean ruler-only attribution."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.4","8B.5","8B.6","8B.7","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"World Bank Approves $750 Million to Support Critical Governance Reforms, Transport Infrastructure, and Digital Connectivity in the Democratic Republic of Congo","publisher":"World Bank","publication_date":"2022-06-28","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/press-release/2022/06/28/world-bank-approves-750-million-to-support-critical-governance-reforms-transport-infrastructure-and-digital-connectivity","claim":"The first IDA-financed budget support operation in the DRC since 2005 backed governance reforms, and the transport/connectivity project would upgrade 440 kilometers of climate-resilient roads while laying fiber optic infrastructure along the financed corridors.","locator":"lines 148-156","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official World Bank press release with specific financing and implementation details.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022","ruler_attribution":"Partial: the government’s reform agenda is credited, but the actual projects are World Bank financed and multiyear, so near-term outcomes are not yet proven.","contrary_evidence":["The projects were newly approved, so this is mobilization and planned implementation rather than completed delivery."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.3","8B.6","8B.9","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Empowering Women Entrepreneurs to Boost Economic Transformation in the Democratic Republic of Congo","publisher":"World Bank","publication_date":"2022-05-02","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/press-release/2022/05/02/empowering-women-entrepreneurs-to-boost-economic-transformation-in-the-democratic-republic-of-congo","claim":"The World Bank approved a $300 million project to support women entrepreneurs and MSMEs, create up to 2,500 formal firms, improve access for up to 25,000 women entrepreneurs, and contribute to a projected 28,000 jobs.","locator":"lines 146-152","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official development-bank release with quantified outputs and ministry supervision details.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022","ruler_attribution":"Partial: the project is aligned to the DRC government’s economic transformation agenda, but the direct implementer and financing are heavily external and the jobs are projected, not yet realized.","contrary_evidence":["The claimed jobs and firm creation are projections over five years, so the article shows planned capacity rather than completed 2022 outcomes."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.4","8B.6","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Democratic Republic of Congo Economic Update: Harnessing Growth Through Digital Connectivity to Create Jobs and Reduce Poverty","publisher":"World Bank","publication_date":"2022-10-07","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/press-release/2022/10/07/democratic-republic-of-congo-economic-update","claim":"Despite robust growth, poverty reduction remained elusive and growth benefits were not widely shared, while the DRC faced a stark digital divide and major geographic and socio-economic disparities in access.","locator":"lines 139-143","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official World Bank update summarizing observed 2022 conditions with specific country findings.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022","ruler_attribution":"Indirect: these are national outcomes during Tshisekedi’s tenure, but the article itself emphasizes inherited constraints, external shocks, and structural issues.","contrary_evidence":["Robust growth and resilience to shocks complicate any simple claim of overall failure."],"lenses":["8B.7","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Democratic Republic of Congo Economic Update: Harnessing Growth Through Digital Connectivity to Create Jobs and Reduce Poverty","publisher":"World Bank","publication_date":"2022-10-07","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/press-release/2022/10/07/democratic-republic-of-congo-economic-update","claim":"The government liberalized the telecommunications sector through a new Telecommunications Law with a modern regulatory environment and a universal access goal, but the report said secondary legislation was still needed to operationalize it.","locator":"lines 145-147","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official World Bank update with a concrete policy description and explicit implementation gap.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022","ruler_attribution":"Direct but partial: the reform is credited to the government, yet the report explicitly says execution still required enabling legislation and follow-through.","contrary_evidence":["The need for secondary legislation means the reform was incomplete in 2022."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.6","8B.8"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Democratic Republic of the Congo: Staff Report for the 2022 Article IV Consultation, Second Review Under the Extended Credit Facility Arrangement, Request for Modifications of Performance Criteria, and Financing Assurances Review","publisher":"International Monetary Fund","publication_date":"2022-07-05","url":"https://www.imf.org/en/publications/cr/issues/2022/07/05/democratic-republic-of-the-congo-staff-report-for-the-2022-article-iv-consultation-second-520400","claim":"The IMF said the authorities adopted prudent macroeconomic policies, most visibly by halting central bank financing to the government, and that scaling up structural reforms remained critical for inclusive growth and the business climate.","locator":"lines 274-276","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official IMF country report with explicit macro-policy assessment and reform agenda.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022","ruler_attribution":"Partial: the macro-policy change is attributable to the Tshisekedi government, but the report also stresses structural constraints and the continuing need for reform.","contrary_evidence":["The same report says additional reforms were still needed, so the improvement was real but incomplete."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.3","8B.7","8B.8","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Vaccinodromes, équipes mobiles : la RDC accélère sa campagne de vaccination contre la COVID-19 ciblant 11 millions de personnes entre avril et juin 2022","publisher":"WHO Regional Office for Africa","publication_date":"2022-04-14","url":"https://www.afro.who.int/node/16056","claim":"Kinshasa launched an accelerated COVID-19 vaccination campaign targeting at least 11 million people between April and June 2022, but official data still showed only 890,363 first-dose vaccinations as of 7 April 2022, and the rollout relied on mobile and fixed vaccination sites.","locator":"lines 415-417 and 422","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official WHO regional note with explicit baseline, target, and operational design details.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022","ruler_attribution":"Partial: the campaign is government-led but partner-supported, and the low starting coverage shows the scale of the challenge rather than completed success.","contrary_evidence":["The target was ambitious and the baseline was very low, so the source shows an effort to catch up rather than achieved vaccination coverage."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.6","8B.7","8B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Providing safety nets for the most vulnerable in the Democratic Republic of Congo: Incremental steps with a large footprint","publisher":"World Bank","publication_date":"2023-02-10","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/results/2023/02/10/providing-safety-nets-for-the-most-vulnerable-in-the-democratic-republic-of-congo-incremental-steps-with-a-large-footpri","claim":"By December 2022, the STEP social protection program had benefited 5.8 million people, improved livelihoods for 530,000 beneficiaries, and upgraded 2,185 community infrastructures while using technical public agencies and real-time supervision.","locator":"lines 93-105","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official World Bank results page summarizing measurable outputs through December 2022.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Outcome evidence through December 2022, published in 2023","ruler_attribution":"Partial: the results are real but heavily donor-supported and institutionally mediated, so the president’s role is indirect rather than exclusive.","contrary_evidence":["The project was long-running and donor-financed, so the results are only partly attributable to Tshisekedi’s 2022 stewardship."],"lenses":["8B.3","8B.5","8B.6","8B.7","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Democratic Republic of Congo: World Bank Approves $250 Million to Improve Stability and Resilience in Conflict-Affected Eastern Provinces","publisher":"World Bank","publication_date":"2022-12-22","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/press-release/2022/12/22/democratic-republic-of-congo-world-bank-approves-250-million-to-improve-stability-and-resilience","claim":"A new $250 million grant was set to improve access to community infrastructure and reintegration programs for 3.3 million people in eastern provinces, with provincial-level implementation and substantial funding for capacity-building, income generation, and psychosocial and mental health services.","locator":"lines 24-30","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official World Bank press release with precise beneficiary counts, funding, and implementation design.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022","ruler_attribution":"Partial: the project is aligned with the government’s renewed commitment to stabilization, but actual results depend on provincial implementation and donor execution.","contrary_evidence":["This is a newly approved grant, so it indicates mobilization and design rather than realized stabilization by year-end."],"lenses":["8B.3","8B.5","8B.6","8B.9","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Congo increases budget 46% for 2023, boosted by taxes","publisher":"Reuters","publication_date":"2022-12-16","url":"https://www.marketscreener.com/news/latest/Congo-increases-budget-46-for-2023-boosted-by-taxes-42566231/","claim":"The DRC increased its 2023 budget to $16 billion, up from a proposed $14.6 billion in September, with the final increase attributed to revenue mobilization and higher mining prices.","locator":"lines 841-880","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting syndicated through MarketScreener with explicit budget numbers and attribution, though not a primary government text.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Late 2022 budget setting for 2023","ruler_attribution":"Partial: revenue mobilization by government services is cited, but commodity prices also helped drive the increase.","contrary_evidence":["Part of the increase came from mining price improvement, so the budget gain is not purely evidence of ruler skill."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.7","8B.10"]}

**Search and rejection summary**
I reviewed roughly 30 documents across presidential pages, Actualite.cd, World Bank, IMF, WHO, Reuters syndications, UNICEF, and related local coverage. I kept 15 distinct URLs and collapsed repeated coverage of the same 145-territories, education, vaccination, and budget stories into single claim units.

Removed or downgraded material fell into these buckets:
- Duplicative syndications of the same Reuters story.
- Out-of-period items from 2023-2026 unless they explicitly reported 2022 outcomes.
- Generic country background pages or broad institutional summaries that did not add a ruler-specific 2022 execution nexus.
- Planning documents, tenders, and launches that were useful only when paired with a separate implementation or outcome source.
- Sources that were relevant to welfare or corruption chapters but did not materially illuminate program execution for 8B.

**Remaining gaps**
- I still do not have hard 2022 evidence that the major 145-territories program was completed at scale; most evidence shows planning, tendering, and early implementation.
- Direct evidence of Tshisekedi personally replacing weak implementers, disciplining laggards, or correcting failed tactics is thin.
- Several of the strongest execution/outcome sources are donor-financed or partner-run, so attribution to Tshisekedi is real but partial.
- More search would help on procurement awards, completed infrastructure, and independent year-end audit or monitoring results for the 145-territories, vaccination, and stabilization tracks.

No score assigned.
